# Flat node_modules instead of pnpm's default symlinked .pnpm store.
#
# Required on Windows for the Android build. pnpm's default layout puts every
# package under a directory named after its full resolution, e.g.
#   node_modules/.pnpm/expo-modules-core@3.0.30_react-native@0.81.5_@babel+core@7.29.7_@types+react@19.1.17_react@19.1.0__react@19.1.0/node_modules/expo-modules-core
# The Android Gradle Plugin then writes build intermediates *inside* that path
# (…/android/build/intermediates/cxx/Debug/<hash>/logs/<abi>/prefab_command.bat),
# which reaches 273 characters — past Windows' 260-char CreateProcess limit.
# Gradle can create the .bat but not execute it:
#   Cannot run program "…\prefab_command.bat": CreateProcess error=2
#
# Hoisting flattens those to node_modules/expo-modules-core/…, roughly 120
# characters shorter, which clears the limit with plenty of margin. This is the
# standard React Native + pnpm arrangement on Windows.
#
# Trade-off: hoisting removes pnpm's strict dependency isolation, so a package
# can import something it never declared. Keep an eye out if a build works
# locally but fails on EAS.
node-linker=hoisted
